1
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:09,170
B1.

2
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:14,400
Toby, the exchange student, will go back to the USA soon.

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,870
David and Nora are planning a goodbye party for him.

4
00:00:18,870 --> 00:00:25,330
Listen to their plan and complete Nora's notes below.

5
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:31,370
Toby is going back to the USA next week.

6
00:00:31,370 --> 00:00:34,470
Shall we have a goodbye party for him?

7
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:37,890
That's a good idea.

8
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:40,810
When shall we have the party?

9
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:43,560
How about this Saturday?

10
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:46,840
That's the 12th of May.

11
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:51,470
Saturday the 12th of May. OK.

12
00:00:51,470 --> 00:00:56,280
Shall we meet at 6pm? That's fine.

13
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:59,470
But where can we have the party?

14
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:04,460
What about the Star Hotel? Oh no.

15
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:07,090
It's too expensive.

16
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:10,180
How about the school hall?

17
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:12,680
That sounds great.

18
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:16,070
I can ask for Miss Law's help.

19
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:21,140
I hope the school allows us to use it. Me too.

20
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:25,030
Now who shall we invite to the party?

21
00:01:25,030 --> 00:01:28,850
Everyone from our class, of course.

22
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:33,630
But Toby also has some friends in other classes.

23
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:37,690
Let's invite them too. OK.

24
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:42,520
Let's talk about the details later after school.
